WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:27.040
Today we pack our bags and unlock the Russian words that let you talk about journey, tickets and getting from place to place. I'm Olya, and this is Привет, Русский, episode 73. Our word of the day is bilet. Say it with me slowly. Be, let, it means ticket. Picture paying a bill yet before you board, and you will remember this word every time. Now try it yourself. Be, let, with bilet you can already say a full sentence.

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:29.260
я покупаю билет на поезд,

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:31.820
that means I am buying a ticket for the train.

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:33.920
Let us build more travel words.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.360
The place where trains arrive is вокзал.

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:37.820
Walk, ZAL.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:39.360
It means train station.

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:41.640
We are going to the train station becomes

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.220
мы идем на вокзал.

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:44.960
Planes landed at airport.

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:46.360
A airport.

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:47.600
Airport.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:49.800
The plane is flying to the airport

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:51.640
is самолет летит в аэропорт.

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:54.120
Remember, летает from earlier lessons.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:57.320
It helps here because planes летает туда аэропорт.

00:00:57.700 --> 00:00:59.340
You need a passport to travel far.

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:00.660
Pass, port.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:01.620
Passport.

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:03.820
Их have a passport, из у меня есть passport.

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:07.720
Easy to remember because it sounds almost the same as the English word.

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:10.360
Your clothes and books go into a чемодан.

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:11.140
Че?

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:11.680
Модан.

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:12.560
Suitcase.

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:16.140
I put things in the suitcase, из якладу вещи в чемодан.

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:18.820
To reach the вокзал, many people use a machine.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:20.220
Машина.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:20.960
Car.

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:23.680
Выоргуем Байкар и с мы едем на машине.

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:25.980
Эбик Триб и Сколт путешествия.

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:27.720
Пу те шествие.

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:29.100
Джорни Ор Триб.

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:33.180
Да Джорни Тумоско увозлонг и с путешествия в Москву было долгим.

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:39.700
Юрсинг стугедр обогаш, ба-гаш, лагич, моя лагича с Хэви и с мой багаж тяжелый.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.500
Ит Саунс Лэк Бэгич анкерезда сейма идея.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:44.420
You find your way в закарта.

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:46.100
Карта, мэп.

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:48.760
I am looking at the map и с я смотрю на карту.

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:52.420
Now for one grammar idea that makes travel talk much easier.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:55.700
Russian uses different verbs for different ways of moving.

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:58.700
Я еду на поезде, means I am going by train.

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:01.700
Мы летим на самолете, means we are flying by plane.

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:03.980
Ты идёшь пешком, means you are walking.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:09.040
Each method gets its own verb, so your sentence tells the listener exactly how the trip happens.

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:12.160
There is something really cool about one of today's words.

00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:16.100
Vagzal begins the name of a London pleasure garden called Voxhall.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:24.240
Инглис инжиниер сброд The Sound to Russia when the first big train stations were built and Russians made it their own ward for any major railway station.

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:27.340
It is a fun borrowing that now feels completely Russian.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:30.020
Just remember, it is not a park anymore.

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:35.660
Picture a grand station with a big V that Russians pronounced their way and the word sticks.

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:41.400
Russians enjoy long train rides, especially on the Trans-Aberian railway that crosses the whole country.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:45.340
Фамилий, Софан пак, Биксома, Варсов, Ти и играть в годы,

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:47.920
так что джорний itself become a part of the fun.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:51.200
Лет as practice, can you remember what Wazal means?

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:52.820
Say it once more,

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:54.220
Вок, Зал,

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:55.420
Трейн Station,

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:58.560
for a quick challenge, draw a simple map of your town.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:02:59.940
Label the Wagsal,

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:01.480
I report and your machine.

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:03.040
Then say out loud,

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:04.440
Я еду на машине.

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:05.900
You did great today.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:08.320
Say today's words out loud one more time

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:09.120
and there yours.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:13.320
share the show with a friend who wants to learn Russian, and I'll see you next time.

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:13.960
Пока!

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:19.800
And if you'd rather watch than listen, find us on youtube at nera-ruu, links in the show notes.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:23.220
